# TypeScript Rules

- Strict TypeScript.
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` and proper narrowing.
- Prefer explicit domain types.
- Separate API DTOs from domain models.
- Use mappers at API boundaries.
- Avoid unsafe type assertions and non-null assertions unless justified.
- Prefer discriminated unions for state machines and variant data.
- Do not leak backend snake_case naming into domain/UI models unless there is a specific reason.
- Use Zod or equivalent runtime schemas for untrusted external data.
- Avoid magic values; use named constants/enums where appropriate.
